First Unique Character in a String
Exercise

Given a string s, find the index of the first character that appears exactly once.

If no such character exists, return -1.

Examples:

s = "leetcode"

Output: 0
s = "loveleetcode"

Output: 2
s = "aabb"

Output: -1


Solution:

let s = "leetcode";
let map = new Map();
let char = "";

for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {
  map.set(s[i], (map.get(s[i]) || 0) + 1);
}

for (let [key, value] of map) {
  if (value === 1) {
    char = key;
    break;
  }
}

console.log(s.indexOf(char));
